{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork","id":1520580,"title":"now that's **** teamwork!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-14T03:43:04-07:00","id":1520580,"title":"now that's **** teamwork!","content":"Ok, i made the mistake of re-reading the teamwork rules for spellcasting (2e core of 119) and found them wanting so here is a comprehensive list of rules and suggested homebrews all in one place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T03:45:46-07:00","id":1520581,"title":"","content":"Teamwork for ritual spells works the same as normal teamwork, but instant casting speed spells do not benefit (see casting time 2e core pg 114).<br /> <br /> Mages without any dots in the spell's highest arcanum, along with sleepwalkers, promixi <s>and sleepers</s> may assist in the casting by helping with ritual chanting, lighting incense, or other appropriate activities relevant to the ritual. They collectively counts as an environment yantra bonus (+1 dice).<br /> <br /> Mages with at least 1 dot in the spell's highest arcanum (**should this be all required Arcana?) May roll a dice pool of Gnosis -3 (untrained penalty) providing any successes as bonus dice to the primary caster.<br /> <br /> Mages able to cast the entire spell may roll as normal, adding any successes as bonus dice to the primary caster.<br /> <br /> Each secondary participant must roll for paradox, and any uncontained paradox will affect the final spell (allowing for clever mage/Scelesti to sabotage the endeavour).<br /> <br /> (See pg 119 of 2e core rules).<br /> <br /> Other ways to help:<br /> <br /> Life: Body Control (see pg 148/149 2e core) metabolism control reduces the need for bio breaks/sleep (may be useful for longer rituals, especially at low Gnosis)<br /> (add combined Mind to remove the need for sleep).<br /> <br /> Prime: As Above, So Below (see pg 166 2e core) granting secondary caster(s) 9/8-again on their yantras to help increase the number of successes.<br /> <br /> Mind: Ritual focus (see pg 55 SoS)<br /> <br /> Time: Choose the threads (see pg 187 2e core)<br /> <br /> Death: Ritual Attunement (homebrew, see Below).<br /> <br /> Cf advanced rules from SoS (pg55) which are (optionally) really good.<br /> <br /> Also for Mysterium member see their order merit's first dot (pg 101 2e core).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":"paste error 08-15-2023, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T03:52:31-07:00","id":1520582,"title":"","content":"Homebrew:<br /> <br /> Ritual Attunement<br /> Death (\u2022\u2022) Ruling<br /> Primary factor: duration<br /> Suggested rote skills: Crafts, Occult, Persuasion<br /> <br /> By making their souls more attuned the mage may help ritual practicioners synchronize their performance. Adds 1 die for any secondary caster assisting with a ritual spellcasting.<br /> <br /> This spell must last the duration of the ritual, otherwise the lose of Attunement will reduce all secondary spellcaster's die pools by -2 (see also interruption rules, SoS pg 56)<br /> <br /> +1 reach: the combined soul Auras makes the seperate signature nimbuses more difficult to discern. Surface information about a spell cast while under the effect of this reach will reveal a single Nimbus which appear to be a mixture of all the casters combined (deep information will still reveal the seperate nimbuses).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  Edited based on the feedback from below, also changed the suggested rote skills to be more in line with the spell 08-15-2023, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T07:32:19-07:00","id":1520589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork#post1520580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, i made the mistake of re-reading the teamwork rules for spellcasting (2e core of 119) and found them wanting</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on that?\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork?p=1520582#post1520582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ritual Attunement<br /> Death (\u2022\u2022) Ruling<br /> Primary factor: duration<br /> Suggested rote skills: Stealth, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> By making their souls more attuned the mage may help ritual practicioners perform more synchronized. The subjects may add 1 die per potency of the spell to any empathy checks between them and other subjects. And adds 1 die for any secondary caster assisting with a ritual spellcasting.<br /> <br /> This spell must last the duration of the ritual, otherwise the sudden change will reduce all secondary spellcaster's die pools by -2.<br /> <br /> +1 reach: When used during a Supernal Summoning, the subjects may be attuned to a single path. This negated the usual modifier for mage from the wrong path being present.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Death might be an Arcanum concerned with souls, but it feels like an unfitting choice for what the effect of a spell such as this would be. Bonuses to Empathy checks feel distinctly out of place with Arcanum and the overall focus of the spell's effect, and possibly functionally useless if they're all engaged in a ritual spellcasting for the duration.<br /> <br /> I also feel as though an extra distinction about the spell needing to be as long as the ritual is a bit pointless, considering how rituals only make a single roll anyway. It doesn't really make much sense that somebody would cast a spell to coordinate a team for only one hour when it's going to take another two hours after that before they even make their roll, because then they got nothing out of it at all. For that matter, the description of a &quot;sudden&quot; change seems odd, when it's likely that it would be a long time after the spell before they even get around to making their rolls.<br /> <br /> Actually, not just likely; at minimum, a ritual could take three hours against a one hour spell, in which case the spell ends prematurely and they've got that amount of time to recover from it. It only takes one step higher on the extended duration chart to make a spell last a day, which is longer than any ritual is capable of being (and considering that you've made this have Duration as the primary factor, even though Potency is the main thing it benefits from, all it takes is one Reach to ensure this spell lasts for a day by default). It feels like a bit of an unnecessary detail when I think most people can be assumed to recognise that a spell such as this is something that has to work across a ritual, rather than be tossed in for a few turns at the end or something.<br /> <br /> Being able to make it so that other mages don't count as different Paths feels like it would be a bit beyond the scope of Death 2, given the nature of Supernal Summoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T08:07:36-07:00","id":1520592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork#post1520580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, i made the mistake of re-reading the teamwork rules for spellcasting (2e core of 119) and found them wanting so here is a comprehensive list of rules and suggested homebrews all in one place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fuck are you talking about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T08:14:14-07:00","id":1520593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork?p=1520592#post1520592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fuck are you talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have elaborated in a post which was taken by the automoderation gods.<br /> <br /> Not reporting it yet. But in brief.<br /> <br /> If you read the teamwork section it suggests all spells can benefit, not just ritual spells. And you have to go and read page 114 to find that limitation (rather than the reference you are guided to for how teamwork works for non-magical spells).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T08:28:47-07:00","id":1520596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork?p=1520593#post1520593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have elaborated in a post which was taken by the automoderation gods.<br /> <br /> Not reporting it yet. But in brief.<br /> <br /> If you read the teamwork section it suggests all spells can benefit, not just ritual spells. And you have to go and read page 114 to find that limitation (rather than the reference you are guided to for how teamwork works for non-magical spells).</div> </div> </div> </div>Riiiiight.<br /> <br /> So for the purposes of getting everyone on board, Teamwork as a mechanic is listed on pages 114 as part of the casting time rules, 119 as part of the Down and Dirty Spellcasting section, and 214 as part of the list for dice pool permutations.<br /> <br /> So by and large the failure of 119 to mention the need to have teamwork for spells be confined to ritual workings comes from the fact that you read page 114 before you read 119, so you already know about the limitation of teamwork to ritual spells in advance before getting into the technical questions about how teamwork works on spells, soooooooooooooooooo.<br /> <br /> the fuck you talking about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T09:04:13-07:00","id":1520598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork?p=1520589#post1520589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you elaborate on that?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Just annoyed (again) when re-reading, to find not all the rules in one place.<br /> <br /> The rules are really clear, but not in one place, so read in isolation that can lead to confusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Death might be an Arcanum concerned with souls, but it feels like an unfitting choice for what the effect of a spell such as this would be. Bonuses to Empathy checks feel distinctly out of place with Arcanum and the overall focus of the spell's effect, and possibly functionally useless if they're all engaged in a ritual spellcasting for the duration. </div> </div> </div> the bonus to empathy is based on the spell Supress Aura. It is not the primary intention of the spell just a flavourful side effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also feel as though an extra distinction about the spell needing to be as long as the ritual is a bit pointless, considering how rituals only make a single roll anyway. It doesn't really make much sense that somebody would cast a spell to coordinate a team for only one hour when it's going to take another two hours after that before they even make their roll, because then they got nothing out of it at all. For that matter, the description of a &quot;sudden&quot; change seems odd, when it's likely that it would be a long time after the spell before they even get around to making their rolls. </div> </div> </div>The sudden change is to facilitate sabotage (someone disrupting the spell) or interruption (like dispellation).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, not just likely; at minimum, a ritual could take three hours against a one hour spell, in which case the spell ends prematurely and they've got that amount of time to recover from it. It only takes one step higher on the extended duration chart to make a spell last a day, which is longer than any ritual is capable of being (and considering that you've made this have Duration as the primary factor, even though Potency is the main thing it benefits from, all it takes is one Reach to ensure this spell lasts for a day by default). </div> </div> </div>You might have a point about the primary factor, i just didn't want to add [potency] dice pool bonus to the secondary spell casters because that feels overpowered.<br /> <br /> And needing to last for ritual duration, duration primary seemed to make sense.<br /> <br /> What would you suggest?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &lt;Snip&gt;<br /> <br /> Being able to make it so that other mages don't count as different Paths feels like it would be a bit beyond the scope of Death 2, given the nature of Supernal Summoning. </div> </div> </div>Yes, actually this should probably be a reach effect of Suppress Aura. Not counting as the path you are from for the purpose of Supernal Summoning.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T10:47:14-07:00","id":1520600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork?p=1520598#post1520598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the bonus to empathy is based on the spell Supress Aura. It is not the primary intention of the spell just a flavourful side effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally tend to lean on the idea that Awakened magic tends not to come with side effects, barring the occasional thing accomplished by Reach. I can see the thing for Suppress Aura based on a general idea of what it means for a person's sense of outwards expression to be Veiled like that, but don't think it should be considered a comprehensive implication of what some things involving souls or auras are like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sudden change is to facilitate sabotage (someone disrupting the spell) or interruption (like dispellation).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that kind of thing is already handily accomplished just by taking away the bonus dice provided by the spell effect, and the idea of making it even more severe by some kind of backlash is both overboard and not really consistent with how magic tends to be portrayed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might have a point about the primary factor, i just didn't want to add [potency] dice pool bonus to the secondary spell casters because that feels overpowered.<br /> <br /> And needing to last for ritual duration, duration primary seemed to make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>On reflection, I think your reasoning was both more correct and what seems to be consistent with choices for primary factor in most events (and particularly that the kinds of bonus dice this provides would be a tad much if they got a lot of them for free).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, actually this should probably be a reach effect of Suppress Aura. Not counting as the path you are from for the purpose of Supernal Summoning.<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the interference caused in summoning by the presence of an alien Path runs far deeper than the presence of their aura or Nimbus, and is not the kind of thing averted simply by Veiling it (or even transforming it). I think it's the actual substance of the connection to the Supernal itself, operating at a level that conventional Practices cannot touch.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T12:15:33-07:00","id":1520602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork?p=1520600#post1520600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally tend to lean on the idea that Awakened magic tends not to come with side effects, barring the occasional thing accomplished by Reach. I can see the thing for Suppress Aura based on a general idea of what it means for a person's sense of outwards expression to be Veiled like that, but don't think it should be considered a comprehensive implication of what some things involving souls or auras are like.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I say side effect, i am thinking of the example Suppress Aura, it seems the main use would be to making a Mage appear to be a sleeper, and the method (suppressing the aura, rather than using Prime to alter it a little more subtly) happens to also make empathy checks worse.<br /> <br /> But I think your point it think is valid, a [potency] dice pool modifier looks more like the primary effect, and further, maybe having a similar aura shouldn't make you easier to empathize with (whereas not being able to get a feel for their aura with the veiling effect it makes sense that the normal empathy becomes harder).<br /> <br /> Thanks for the constructive feedback (i will edit it later)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would think that kind of thing is already handily accomplished just by taking away the bonus dice provided by the spell effect, and the idea of making it even more severe by some kind of backlash is both overboard and not really consistent with how magic tends to be portrayed. </div> </div> </div>I think that is a fair comment, magic in general doesn't result in a backslash, i was thinking of this in terms of being interrupted in the middle of a ritual, which i think SoS has rules for (on page 55?) But I haven't re-read them today, so the detail escapes me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On reflection, I think your reasoning was both more correct and what seems to be consistent with choices for primary factor in most events (and particularly that the kinds of bonus dice this provides would be a tad much if they got a lot of them for free). </div> </div> </div>The only issue then is that a ritual usually takes 1 scene, (even if that is 3 hours, but even then that is Gnosis 1-2, most rituals are conducted in less time, maybe even Gnosis 9-10 ritual with 5 extra intervals) so primary duration gets you very little - unless you are doing multiple rituals with the same group in the course of a week, say.<br /> <br /> It still feels right, especially as i think i will remove the potency effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the interference caused in summoning by the presence of an alien Path runs far deeper than the presence of their aura or Nimbus, and is not the kind of thing averted simply by Veiling it (or even transforming it). I think it's the actual substance of the connection to the Supernal itself, operating at a level that conventional Practices cannot touch. </div> </div> </div>That seems reasonable from a metaphysics perspective. The Supernal connection of your path is beyond Space and Death (though i suppose you could argue removing their soul until they can't cast magic might break it)<br /> <br /> I think either way would be fine to run at your own table. But I think I will remove this reach for now.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to add a reach effect, what would you suggest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T12:45:28-07:00","id":1520606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork?p=1520602#post1520602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that is a fair comment, magic in general doesn't result in a backslash, i was thinking of this in terms of being interrupted in the middle of a ritual, which i think SoS has rules for (on page 55?) But I haven't re-read them today, so the detail escapes me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interruption (which seems to be particular in terms of the mage actually needing to redirect attention and energy to do something else, rather than just incidental intrusions) is stated to inflict a -3 penalty on actions that the mage attempts to do while holding on to the complete Imago, and inflict a -1 penalty on the casting pool per minute not performing the ritual (with potential to break the imago if the pool drops to zero).<br /> <br /> I'll admit, I do think that does provide a precedent for something occurring during a ritual casting that mars attempts to form an imago across the entire rest of the casting, regardless of how long it might be. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only issue then is that a ritual usually takes 1 scene, (even if that is 3 hours</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the lowest extended duration being listed as scene/hour speaks more to the idea that such spells can last less than an hour in cases where a scene would be so short and it makes sense for it to only last for such a dramatic sequence, but doesn't necessarily mean that any amount of time that could be regarded as a single scene is valid for such a duration. Especially if it exceeds an hour by a noteworthy amount of time.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I think the advantage that one would seek from extra duration wouldn't be lasting across the whole ritual so much as being valid for multiple rituals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems reasonable from a metaphysics perspective. The Supernal connection of your path is beyond Space and Death (though i suppose you could argue removing their soul until they can't cast magic might break it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, I think that given references to the way that Gnosis works, it could be said that a mage who has been reduced to the Thrall Condition still has their Path, they just can't do anything with it (or at least can't cast spells; strictly speaking, nothing says that they can't utilise other aspects of the mage template). After all, if they can still cast spells in the absence of the soul for a while, I'd say <i>something</i> must still be connecting to the Supernal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted to add a reach effect, what would you suggest?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure... keeping with it being under Death, possibly something to do with Willpower for aiding the spell. Although I'm not sure what would be useful beyond everybody already being able to spend Willpower to add dice to their pools before seeing how many successes they can transmit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T14:03:12-07:00","id":1520611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork?p=1520606#post1520606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interruption (which seems to be particular in terms of the mage actually needing to redirect attention and energy to do something else, rather than just incidental intrusions) is stated to inflict a -3 penalty on actions that the mage attempts to do while holding on to the complete Imago, and inflict a -1 penalty on the casting pool per minute not performing the ritual (with potential to break the imago if the pool drops to zero).<br /> <br /> I'll admit, I do think that does provide a precedent for something occurring during a ritual casting that mars attempts to form an imago across the entire rest of the casting, regardless of how long it might be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counting it as an interuption (until the souls could be re-attuned) would be very harsh, but simplify the spell description.<br /> <br /> What would a comparison be? Breaking runes or stealing someone's dedicated magical tool in the middle of a ritual? Though that would just take the dice pool bonus away?<br /> <br /> Stealing a sympathy yantra which is necessary for sympatethic casting, which could ruin the spell (or force them to pick a new subject?).<br /> <br /> So the -3 pentaly would apply to casting anything else (can you even hold two imagos at the same time?) Or for noticing someone sneakily messing with your dedicated magical tool, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the lowest extended duration being listed as scene/hour speaks more to the idea that such spells can last less than an hour in cases where a scene would be so short and it makes sense for it to only last for such a dramatic sequence, but doesn't necessarily mean that any amount of time that could be regarded as a single scene is valid for such a duration. Especially if it exceeds an hour by a noteworthy amount of time. </div> </div> </div>I wasn't sure, but i was going to add that the book rarely says [1 scene/hour]. For example i would have assumed that using Shifting Sands to go back 24 hours requires 24 reach. But it says 1 reach gives you 1 scene extra...<br /> <br /> This is i think the one case where 1 scene/hour <b><u>is</u></b> used. But I don't see where it says to use the lower... Is that in the storytelling section?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With that in mind, I think the advantage that one would seek from extra duration wouldn't be lasting across the whole ritual so much as being valid for multiple rituals. </div> </div> </div>\ud83d\udc4d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really, I think that given references to the way that Gnosis works, it could be said that a mage who has been reduced to the Thrall Condition still has their Path, they just can't do anything with it (or at least can't cast spells; strictly speaking, nothing says that they can't utilise other aspects of the mage template). After all, if they can still cast spells in the absence of the soul for a while, I'd say <i>something</i> must still be connecting to the Supernal. </div> </div> </div>So you can activate mage sight, though that requires willpower to keep up (more than Gnosis in minutes)... so maybe 0 minutes for a thrall, depending on how much Gnosis they lost (mechanically it is one Gnosis lost everytime you lose a dot of willpower while enervated, so if you have more Gnosis than willpower then, you might still be able to keep active mage sight up).<br /> <br /> What other options? Supernal Summoning while a thrall? Mechanically seems good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can barely muster up the will to do your job anymore, and anything more emotionally intense than a raised voice makes you flinch and back down. Apply a \u20132 to all Social rolls and rolls involving Resolve... </div> </div> </div> along with no willpower, no spells, not bothered using their defence in combat and can't spend any XP.<br /> <br /> Yeah, looks like you could make a connection to the supernal and ask a supernal entity for a new soul... Beating their Trial might be difficult.<br /> <br /> What about non-legacy attainments? If you aren't able to apply defence in combat, raising mage armour seems out of line. And it says when you regain the ability to use legacy attainments (based on the Gnosis returning) so presumably you can use legacy attainments if you had less willpower than Gnosis and still have the minimum required for that attainment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure... keeping with it being under Death, possibly something to do with Willpower for aiding the spell. Although I'm not sure what would be useful beyond everybody already being able to spend Willpower to add dice to their pools before seeing how many successes they can transmit. </div> </div> </div>Is Death keenly associated with willpower? I would have assumed Mind had a better purview for that. Death and the soul (looking at what it can do to souls already - soul marks gives a good idea of what you can see with a Death Unveiling, but nothing sticks out as being useful to Ruling with Death to help...) I can't really see anything else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T00:21:56-07:00","id":1520648,"title":"","content":"Ok, my second post is back (and edited too) and I've updated the homebrew Death spell. That is for the feedback <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T12:09:52-07:00","id":1520694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork?p=1520592#post1520592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fuck are you talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\"><b>This is really uncalled for, take a posting break. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T15:29:04-07:00","id":1520718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork?p=1520611#post1520611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is Death keenly associated with willpower?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking in terms of something akin to Devouring the Slain there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T13:59:36-07:00","id":1520789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1520580-now-that-s-teamwork?p=1520718#post1520718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking in terms of something akin to Devouring the Slain there.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an effect it seems more in line with Mind, doing it with Death seems like it is pattern scouring, i suppose you could have the whole ritual group agree to take 1 lethal damage in exchange for granting them a willpower (or the lethal damage could be to some other ritual participants, maybe sleepwalkers).<br /> <br /> I like that as an alternative spell; particularily harsh if one sleepwalker takes multiple lethal damage to grant the Mages willpower. Ideally you don't kill your sleepwalker and give them time to recover between rituals...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}